{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["יְנָחֵנִי — הִנְחֵנִי." "From the mountains of the east — a doubled expression, for it is written: אֲרַם מִקֶּדֶם — that is: great effort from a distant land. And for nothing, for it will avail him nothing." "זַעֲמָה — it appears to me: the zayin with pataḥ, so that it is an imperative form. But זוֹעֲמָה with holem would yield the feminine of 'angry,' as in אֵשׁ אֹכְלָה. And she judges Israel."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:50:50.346594117Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}